# setuptools' legacy sdist default matches only tests/test*.py, which silently
# omitted tests/conftest.py and tests/__init__.py. The shipped 0.2.0 sdist then
# produced 72 passed / 85 errors — every test depending on a fixture failed at
# setup with "fixture 'cdfi_fa_award' not found". Anyone auditing
# cdfi-fund-tracker from PyPI saw a broken test suite for a release whose entire
# claim is that it fails loudly instead of fabricating data.
#
# Third instance of this defect in the portfolio: sbic-tracker recorded
# "26 passed / 57 errors" and oz-tracker "No module named 'tests.conftest'",
# both fixed three days before this one. The fix was written twice and
# propagated nowhere, so this release also adds a release-pipeline job that
# unpacks the built sdist and runs ITS suite — the MANIFEST.in is only what
# makes that job pass. Packaging that is never installed from is packaging that
# is never verified.
recursive-include tests *.py

include README.md
include CHANGELOG.md
include pyproject.toml
include setup.py

global-exclude *.pyc __pycache__/*
